signed a bunch of meaningless

00:10:28.127 --> 00:10:31.296
and unconstitutional executive
orders rather than negotiate

00:10:31.296 --> 00:10:33.599
with Congress while
tens of millions of Americans

00:10:33.599 --> 00:10:35.434
face eviction and go without

00:10:35.434 --> 00:10:37.236
much-needed
unemployment benefits.

00:10:37.236 --> 00:10:40.339
Take, for example, Trump's claim
that he's supposedly

00:10:40.339 --> 00:10:42.874
extending the enhanced
unemployment benefits.

00:10:42.874 --> 00:10:46.312
First of all, he is cutting them
from $600 to $400.

00:10:46.312 --> 00:10:48.680
Second, he is forcing
cash-strapped states

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:52.050
to pay 25% of that amount,
and if they can't,

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:53.886
then their residents
don't get the money.

00:10:53.886 --> 00:10:57.556
And third, even his own economic
advisor Larry Kudlow

00:10:57.556 --> 00:11:01.293
didn't seem to know how any
of this will work at all.

00:11:01.293 --> 00:11:03.929
-So when will people see
their first checks?

00:11:03.929 --> 00:11:08.600
-I don't want to be as specific
as you might hold me to it

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.936
as you should, but I think
it's going to be

00:11:10.936 --> 00:11:12.971
in a couple of weeks,
and I think it's going to

00:11:12.971 --> 00:11:16.975
come to about $1,200 per person.
That's a huge --

00:11:16.975 --> 00:11:19.545
-You keep saying
$1,200 per person.

00:11:19.545 --> 00:11:22.414
Are you talking about in
addition to the unemployment

00:11:22.414 --> 00:11:25.784
that they are already getting?
-Oh, no, that --

00:11:25.784 --> 00:11:28.220
-Where does that number
come from?

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:30.689
-I beg your pardon.

00:11:30.689 --> 00:11:33.359
The $1,200 will come from
the payroll tax.

00:11:33.359 --> 00:11:34.760
It should be 800 bucks.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:38.230
I beg your pardon. It should
be 800 bucks for the employment.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:42.601
-$800 or $400?
-No. It should be four --

00:11:42.601 --> 00:11:44.403
It should be $800.

00:11:44.403 --> 00:11:48.540
If the states step up,
we are prepared to match.

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:53.144
That should come out
$400 Federal, $400 States.

00:11:53.144 --> 00:11:57.816
-Okay. We'll move on
because I think this is --

00:11:57.816 --> 00:12:00.419
it's not what the president
said, and it's a bit confusing.

00:12:00.419 --> 00:12:02.588
-Man, even Dana Bash gave up.

00:12:02.588 --> 00:12:04.556
That was like watching her
sort through the menu

00:12:04.556 --> 00:12:06.057
at a restaurant with
her grandfather.

00:12:06.057 --> 00:12:07.126
You want the chicken?

00:12:07.126 --> 00:12:08.394
[ Deep voice ]
No, I want the pollo.

00:12:08.394 --> 00:12:09.628
[ Normal voice ]
Pollo means chicken.

00:12:09.628 --> 00:12:10.996
[ Deep voice ]
I thought it meant fish.

00:12:10.996 --> 00:12:12.765
[ Normal voice ] Pesce is fish.
[ Deep voice ] The actor?

00:12:12.765 --> 00:12:14.834
[ Normal voice ] Just bring him
some French fries, please.

00:12:14.834 --> 00:12:17.870
How can he not know
what his own policy does?

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.505
He sounds like the substitute
math teacher

00:12:19.505 --> 00:12:21.440
who spilled coffee
on his lesson plan.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:24.242
"Okay, everybody,
the answer is $1,200.

00:12:24.242 --> 00:12:26.545
No, um, wait, I'm sorry,
it's 8-- Nope.

00:12:26.545 --> 00:12:29.248
I think it's $500. It's $5,000."

00:12:29.248 --> 00:12:30.882
"Mr. Kudlow, I think it's $400."

00:12:30.882 --> 00:12:32.418
"Shut up,
you little snot-nosed punk.

00:12:32.418 --> 00:12:34.954
It's 800. Run to the teachers'
lounge and get me another beer."

00:12:34.954 --> 00:12:37.555
You are not allowed to drink
beer, Mr. Kudlow.

00:12:37.555 --> 00:12:39.824
"Well, don't you just sound
like the superintendent

00:12:39.824 --> 00:12:41.293
who fired me from my last job?"

00:12:41.293 --> 00:12:44.363
And then there's the executive
order that supposedly extends

00:12:44.363 --> 00:12:48.133
the federal eviction moratorium,
which it obviously does not do.

00:12:48.133 --> 00:12:50.335
That's a lie.
All you have to do is read it,

00:12:50.335 --> 00:12:52.538
which apparently Kudlow
has not done.

00:12:52.538 --> 00:12:56.575
-A second key point
was the eviction moratorium.

00:12:56.575 --> 00:13:00.713
Because the Democrats rejected
various compromises

00:13:00.713 --> 00:13:02.915
at least twice, to my knowledge,

00:13:02.915 --> 00:13:05.317
the president felt he had
to take action.

00:13:05.317 --> 00:13:06.752
-In fact,
the president doesn't extend

00:13:06.752 --> 00:13:08.020
the federal eviction moratorium.

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:10.889
I looked at the executive order.
It doesn't do that.

00:13:10.889 --> 00:13:13.025
It simply directs HUD to find
a way to help people

00:13:13.025 --> 00:13:14.393
and identify federal funds.

00:13:14.393 --> 00:13:18.296
It doesn't include extending
the eviction moratorium.

00:13:18.296 --> 00:13:21.400
-Well, look,
that's not entirely true.

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:24.736
I mean, in there...

00:13:24.736 --> 00:13:27.405
-"Oh, come on, George.
That's not fair.

00:13:27.405 --> 00:13:29.808
If I haven't read it,
you can't either."

00:13:29.808 --> 00:13:31.777
It's fun to imagine Kudlow's
aides shuttling in

00:13:31.777 --> 00:13:34.013
from interview to interview
watching him make a fool

00:13:34.013 --> 00:13:36.448
of himself and then hoping
the next one goes better.

00:13:36.448 --> 00:13:39.384
"All right, boss. We have only
one more interview left today."

00:13:39.384 --> 00:13:41.053
"Where is it?
Please say Fox News.

00:13:41.053 --> 00:13:43.588
"Please, Fox News."
"It's, uh, Axios."

00:13:43.588 --> 00:13:46.525
"Oh, damn it. Well, you better
give me some of those

00:13:46.525 --> 00:13:49.728
loose papers that are fun to
carry around and hard to read."

00:13:49.728 --> 00:13:52.831
And then there's Trump's
fake payroll tax cut.

00:13:52.831 --> 00:13:55.034
In reality, all he did
was defer payroll taxes

00:13:55.034 --> 00:13:57.269
until the end of the year,
which means a lot of businesses

00:13:57.269 --> 00:14:00.105
will save up the money to pay
those taxes when they are due

00:14:00.105 --> 00:14:02.607
rather than pass
the savings on to workers.

00:14:02.607 --> 00:14:05.611
Trump said if he was re-elected,
he would make the cut permanent,

00:14:05.611 --> 00:14:07.813
which is even worse
because payroll taxes

00:14:07.813 --> 00:14:09.981
fund Social Security
and Medicare.

00:14:09.981 --> 00:14:13.319
So if you cut payroll taxes
without a replacement,

00:14:13.319 --> 00:14:15.320
you are cutting Social Security.

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:17.189
And when he was asked about
that last night,

00:14:17.189 --> 00:14:19.157
as usual, he just lied.

00:14:19.157 --> 00:14:21.727
-What we're doing is we
reimburse through general fund,

00:14:21.727 --> 00:14:23.194
not through Social Security.

00:14:23.194 --> 00:14:26.565
This will have no impact
on Social Security.

00:14:26.565 --> 00:14:28.967
We are going to impact --
we are going to,

00:14:28.967 --> 00:14:32.604
through the general fund,
reimburse.

00:14:32.604 --> 00:14:35.273
This will have zero impact
on Social Security.

00:14:35.273 --> 00:14:36.675
-That's not how it works.

00:14:36.675 --> 00:14:39.178
For one thing, only Congress
can appropriate money.

00:14:39.178 --> 00:14:40.745
For another, this isn't
one of your businesses.

00:14:40.745 --> 00:14:43.481
You can't move money around
to cover your losses.

00:14:43.481 --> 00:14:44.650
[ As Trump ] I got it.

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:46.118
We're just gonna move money
from the tax fund

00:14:46.118 --> 00:14:48.553
to the casino fund to the
hotel fund to the slush fund

00:14:48.553 --> 00:14:50.221
to the porn star fund,
boom, done.

00:14:50.221 --> 00:14:51.390
[ Normal voice ]
But how do we pay our taxes?

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.391
[ As Trump ]
Oh, that's easy. We don't.

00:14:53.391 --> 00:14:54.927
You guys should really --

00:14:54.927 --> 00:14:56.728
You should really try
tapping on my head.

00:14:56.728 --> 00:14:58.597
It's like silly putty.

00:14:58.597 --> 00:15:00.065
[ Normal voice ] Americans
can see through this.

00:15:00.065 --> 00:15:02.734
It's trump's usual shtick.
He is desperate and unpopular,

00:15:02.734 --> 00:15:05.070
which is why he is signing
empty executive orders

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:06.705
and sabotaging the post office.

00:15:06.705 --> 00:15:09.441
He has no accomplishments,
no policies...

00:15:09.441 --> 00:15:12.544
-No anything.
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:15:12.544 --> 00:15:14.879
And this was the most stressful
one I have done all summer

00:15:14.879 --> 00:15:17.316
because my parents were sitting
on a couch watching.

00:15:25.057 --> 00:15:26.325
[ Sighs ]

